	<entry>
		<title>Madonna broke every record with her Super Bowl Half Time Show</title>
		<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/561-madonna-broke-every-record-with-her-super-bowl-half-time-show.html"/>
		<published>2012-02-06T23:44:28Z</published>
		<updated>2012-02-06T23:44:28Z</updated>
		<id>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/561-madonna-broke-every-record-with-her-super-bowl-half-time-show.html</id>
		<author>
			<name>Giampiero Fiorelli</name>
		</author>
		<summary type="html">&lt;div class=&quot;K2FeedIntroText&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;This year's &lt;strong&gt;Super Bowl&lt;/strong&gt; has been the most watched program in TV history, with more than 111.3 milion people on average. And &lt;strong&gt;Madonna's Half Time&lt;/strong&gt; performance averaged 114 million people. Last night game averaged an impressive 47.8 rating in the U.S., while &lt;strong&gt;Madonna&lt;/strong&gt;'s show received 48.3.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It was originally reported that &lt;strong&gt;Madonna&lt;/strong&gt;'s performance during the &lt;strong&gt;Super Bowl's Halftime Show&lt;/strong&gt; saw an average of 8,000 Tweets per second for five minutes. But the exact data is that &lt;strong&gt;Madonna&lt;/strong&gt;'s &lt;strong&gt;Super Bowl&lt;/strong&gt; performance Caused 10,245 Tweets per second. Her performance placed #2 for most hits per second of all times.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Madonna&lt;/strong&gt; peaked at 20:09 EST with a 7000% spike in social activity, according to AddThis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But &lt;strong&gt;Madonna&lt;/strong&gt; broke another - quite impossible - record: the big majority of international press praised her performance. Also, hostile American audience had to admit that they really enjoyed her performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;According to what Google just revealed, it was neither the Giants nor Patriots that people were searching for most last night on Google during the game: it was &lt;strong&gt;Madonna&lt;/strong&gt;. Overall, the top trending searches on Google during the Super Bowl last night were:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Madonna &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Halftime show &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Patriots &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tom Brady &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Giants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Above all the players, &lt;strong&gt;Madonna&lt;/strong&gt; took the spotlight as the  most-searched term during the game.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: medium;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: 'book antiqua',palatino;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</summary>
